WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.340
This is a narration generated by artificial intelligence to accompany the study of John, chapter four.

00:00:07.340 --> 00:00:10.066
Images are artistic illustrations.

00:00:10.066 --> 00:00:11.324
Verses 1 to 6.

00:00:11.324 --> 00:00:14.120
Jesus leaves Judea and stops in Samaria.

00:00:14.120 --> 00:00:21.111
Upon learning of the reaction of the Pharisees, Jesus leaves Judea and proceeds to Galilee, passing through Samaria.

00:00:21.111 --> 00:00:30.408
The text highlights that he tires, sits by the well of Jacob and finds a Samaritan woman in a common but decisive moment.

00:00:30.408 --> 00:00:31.769
Verses 7 to 26.

00:00:31.769 --> 00:00:35.775
The dialogue on living water and true worship.

00:00:35.775 --> 00:00:44.241
Jesus transforms a simple request for water into a revelation about the gift of God, human thirst, and eternal life.

00:00:44.241 --> 00:00:56.638
He also confronts the woman's moral history and corrects the discussion about the correct place of worship, pointing to worship the Father in spirit and in truth.

00:00:56.638 --> 00:01:00.720
The climax comes when he identifies himself as the Messiah.

00:01:00.720 --> 00:01:02.262
Verses 27 to 42.

00:01:02.262 --> 00:01:06.075
The testimony of the woman and the faith of the Samaritans.

00:01:06.075 --> 00:01:13.946
The disciples strange the conversation, but the woman leaves her cantaro, goes to the city and calls the people.

00:01:13.946 --> 00:01:21.574
Jesus teaches that his true food is to do the will of the Father and speaks of the already mature harvest.

00:01:21.574 --> 00:01:29.688
Many Samaritans first believe by the testimony of the woman and then by the word of Jesus himself.

00:01:29.688 --> 00:01:31.112
Verses 43 to 54.

00:01:31.112 --> 00:01:35.457
Jesus returns to Galilee and performs the second sign in Cana.

00:01:35.457 --> 00:01:40.252
After two days between the Samaritans, Jesus goes to Galilee.

00:01:40.252 --> 00:01:47.370
In Cana, an officer asks for the healing of his son, and Jesus calls him to believe without requiring physical presence.

00:01:47.370 --> 00:01:53.963
The man believes in the word of Jesus before seeing the result, and all his house believes too.

00:01:53.963 --> 00:01:57.785
John concludes that this was the second sign in Cana.

00:01:57.785 --> 00:02:05.352
